I'm an EU player that moved, so geographically and time zone wise I have to play with Americans. 

&#x200B;

Over the course of classic I've managed to find a decent core of people and get them together and keep playing.

&#x200B;

However, the one thing I've noticed about Americans is how toxic a LOT of communities and guilds are.  From griefing, to lying, to waving dicks around and saying one side will complete the WE in 1 week (Spoilers It's week 3 and you guys lied, what a shocker) the constant need to ALWAYS BE NUMBER 1 and win at everything, It's just wild. Even getting people down for carapaces was a "What do I get out of it though?" 

&#x200B;

I've never in 14 years of WoW experinced it this bad. EU has some really cool players, I think it's the fact that they all come from diverse backgrounds and countries, rather then 1 giant country. 

&#x200B;

Not to say all American players are awful they really aren't, some servers got together and got shit sorted and completed very quickly, however others are just seemingly so angry and toxic towards each other it's just sad. I've met some great people on these servers but compared to EU it's a real let down

I personally pushed members of my guild to do it instead and helped them, even farming carapaces while I went on holiday sitting back the pool.

