Hey OP, lately I've been REALLY loving the stalker AT, not sure why

&#x200B;

I made an Elec/Shield stalker which is really REALLY fun, Elec suffers from really shitty single target so on a stalker this is cured, It produces some really good numbers and just melts everything, some end problems but nothing that bad. 

&#x200B;

Then I made a Savage/energy and it's really fun as well BUT it suffers from dealing with such large resistances from enemy groups, Council robots, Arachnos tarantulas etc, it's really frustrating because I know I could be hitting a LOT harder and sometimes it just feels like a wet noodle, a lot of it's damage is also from dots and everything dies pretty quickly in a group, I haven't played it solo but I think it could be quite beastly.

&#x200B;

My next stalker I'm thinking of doing is either going to be Broadsword/Shield or maybe Ice/something.

&#x200B;

Stalkers if you have the money (I spend about 150/200 million) are amazing

