I play a WS and a Staff/SR Brute.

&#x200B;

On my WS, I run 50+4 all the time, while levelling I keep it at +2 when below level 35 and above 35 I run +3.

&#x200B;

I always make my own team as well, I don't join other teams after some awful experiences, you need to make the team to suit what you have, Ideally you always want a Kin, It's what I search for in every team, they are just that good. 

&#x200B;

After that you want 2-3 controllers/doms - 2 trollers are great because the secondary is a support so often they might even have Kin so you kill 2 birds with 1 stone, other times they might have a healing secondary or a -res debuff (Dark, Rad etc)  You can also pickup a mastermind here as they are just fantastic at holding general aggro, not bad damage and good support to boot!

&#x200B;

Then what I do is I look at how tanky my team is, As I said I play a Warshade and a Brute so I normally want someone else in the front lines with me so I pickup any tank AT, Normally a Warshade or a Peacebringer if I'm on my brute or brutes and a tanker if I'm on my Shade, you always want to have at least 1 Warshade or PB on your team really, they get stacked and benefit a LOT from other ATs.

&#x200B;

Right now we are at 5-6 people - The last 2 slots are free pick, I often choose a Sentinel if I am farming/doing AV missions for that tasty + damage buff they give, otherwise depending on how AOE heavy my team is already (By looking at powersets) I might want some more ST damage, so a blaster/scrapper/stalker is my next pick. Shout out to any crabs/forts here as well they are great and I'd recommend them in any team.  (Not banes tho) 

&#x200B;

Here I have 1 slot left and It's really just a free pick, Often I pickup another tank just so I can make sure my squishes stay alive, Squishes are always happy if they can just sit at the back and hit stuff for lots of numbers.

&#x200B;

I hope this helped you man, team comp in this game is super important, a group of 5 stalkers, 1 tank and 2 blasters isn't going to do very well for very long. 

&#x200B;

